          {
            title: 'Sedma',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Sedma is a Czech trick-and-draw card game in which tricks are won by matching ranks; sevens act as wild cards. The game originated in Bohemia and became one of the most popular games in Czechoslovakia, and is played in partnerships or by 2–3 players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Bohemia (Czech Republic). Sedma is a Czech trick-and-draw game; it may have originated in Hungary or Poland and spread to Czechoslovakia in the mid-20th century, becoming one of the most popular games there. Related games exist across Central and Eastern Europe (Sedmice, Șeptică, Zsírozás, Hola).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
